// endpoint_subscribe_workspace.proto — SubscribeWorkspace: tell one
// workspace's agent when another workspace changes. AGENT API section.
//
// FOR AGENTS, NOT PROGRAMS. An agent's call ends with its command, long before
// the change it waits for, so a subscription is not a stream: the daemon holds
// it and delivers each notice to the SUBSCRIBER's session as a deferred prompt
// of origin conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_WORKSPACE_NOTICE, the
// path a merge-queue notice takes: it waits behind a running turn, wakes an
// idle agent, and the feed draws no row for it. Each notice names the change
// and carries the followed workspace's status after it (WorkspaceStatus).
//
// NOTHING SLIPS BETWEEN READING AND FOLLOWING. The answer carries the followed
// workspace's status as it stands when the subscription is taken, and every
// change after that answer is noticed.
//
// SCOPE AND LIFETIME. A subscriber holds AT MOST ONE subscription per followed
// workspace; subscribing again replaces its events. A subscription ends when
// the subscriber unsubscribes, when the SUBSCRIBER closes however it closes
// (re-opening it does not restore it), and when the followed workspace is
// forgotten or nuked. It is DURABLE across a daemon restart and a handover. A
// change made while no daemon serves is never noticed; the next notice's status
// carries its effect.

